35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It's worse than I thought. The car is often left dirty or with the fuel light on, and our weekly routine trips are the ones most likely to collapse.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Recording every run is a nightmare; it took nearly an hour a week just to track everything. Plus, the diary shows we use the car way more on Saturdays than Tuesdays.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The fixed costs are quite significant, totaling over 280,000 yen before fuel. However, I also found that when we tried checking each other's figures, it created a climate of accusation and apology.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Other households said the worst part is asking for favors or people clinging to turns they don't need. Also, those heavy-use weeks cost us whole evenings of trying to work around each other.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The fuel receipts are totally lopsided! Two of us paid for most of it, while one person barely paid anything. Also, the mechanic says short trips are killing the battery and brakes!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, that explains why the car feels so worn out. If we're just doing short trips and leaving it empty, it's no wonder the system is breaking down.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Servas, if checking figures makes us feel accused, then May's ""nightmare"" of recording every run is just adding more stress. We need a system that doesn't feel like a chore or an interrogation.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are caught between the need for precision and the need for peace. If the act of accounting poisons the friendship, perhaps we should seek a simpler path.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, it sounds like the ""favors"" other people talked about are exactly what's happening with our weekly trips. We're relying on each other too much and it's making us grumpy.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, if two people paid for almost all the fuel, that's not fair! But @Servas is right, we can't just start accusing each other or it'll get ugly. We need a way to be fair without fighting!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we keep relying on favors for those weekly trips, they'll just keep collapsing. We need a way to guarantee the car is available and ready for the things we actually count on.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree. If we spend our whole evening coordinating or an hour a week recording runs, we're losing too much. We need a system that minimizes the ""admin"" and the constant negotiating.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must consider that a system requiring constant vigilance may be as costly as the fuel itself. Perhaps a structure that provides certainty without the need for constant verification is the answer.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I think we should avoid anything that makes us feel like we're constantly asking for favors or policing each other. That's exactly what the other households said ruins the mood.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I just want to make sure the person who barely paid for fuel starts chipping in! But I don't want to be the ""bad guy"" who makes everyone feel accused.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We need a solution that ensures the car is clean and fueled for the next person, especially for those of us with fixed weekly commitments.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,Exactly. We need to stop the endless arranging and the tedious tracking. Whatever we choose should just work without us having to spend our whole evening talking about it.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,It is clear that the emotional cost of our current arrangement is as high as the financial one. We must find a balance that preserves our harmony while ensuring no one is unfairly burdened.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I agree. We need a system where we don't have to beg for turns or feel guilty for using the car, because that's what's actually souring our friendship.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you all! Let's find a way to be fair with the money and the fuel, but in a way that keeps us all happy and friends!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
